12132DB2DB794613B62ACD834A5E999C.description:
For a function that models a relationship between two quantities, interpret key features of graphs and tables in
terms of the quantities, and sketch graphs showing key features given a verbal description of the relationship. Key features include: intercepts; intervals where the function is increasing, decreasing, positive, or negative;
relative maximums and minimums; symmetries; end behavior; and periodicity. ★

50C1574F38644111BD4312A7ABA299BA.description:
Explain election processes at the local, state, and federal levels, including qualifications and procedures
for voting; qualifications and terms for offices; the primary system; public hearings and forums; petition,
initiative, referendum, and recall; and amendments related to elections and voting.

B2DF8C60D24F4BB492F5D1C88863B863.description:
Evaluate restrictions and expansions of civil liberties and civil rights in the United States and the role of
the legislative, executive, and judicial branches of the government in related events and developments
over time, including the Thirteenth, Fourteenth, and Fifteenth Amendments; Plessy v. Ferguson (1896);
the Espionage and Sedition Acts; Schenck v. United States (1919); the Nineteenth Amendment;
Executive Order 9066; Executive Order 10730; Brown v. Board of Education (1954); the Civil Rights Act of
1964; the Voting Rights Act of 1965; the Twenty-Fourth Amendment; and Twenty-Sixth Amendment.

12CA123E62A841B281660E5376EC1739.description:
Evaluate the reasoning for Supreme Court decisions and their political, social, and economic effects,
including Marbury v. Madison (1803); McCulloch v. Maryland (1819); Cherokee Nation v. Georgia (1831);
Dred Scott v. Sandford (1857); Plessy v. Ferguson (1896); Schenck v. United States (1919); Korematsu v.
United States (1944); Brown v. Board of Education (1954); Baker v. Carr (1962); Engel v. Vitale (1962);
Gideon v. Wainwright (1963); Miranda v. Arizona (1966); Loving v. Virginia (1967); Tinker v. Des Moines
(1969); New York Times Co. v. United States (1971); Wisconsin v. Yoder (1972); Roe v. Wade (1973);
United States v. Nixon (1974); Shaw v. Reno (1993); United States v. Lopez (1995); Bush v. Gore (2000);
McDonald v. Chicago (2010); Citizens United v. Federal Election Commission (2010).

37C1B852B08444CA9A5BE7BC56B323ED.description:
Obtain, evaluate and communicate information on the effectiveness of management or conservation practices
for one of Louisiana’s natural resources with respect to common considerations such as social, economic,
technological, and influencing political factors over the past 50 years.
